title The door that recorded teaching what it never said
prompt autonomous loop, lap 4205 -- take the next agent-doable lap, reds first
rota lap 4205, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears; listening for the page nobody answered led straight to the doorway census, which was RED at the cold open
think The scoped cold roster opened the lap and answered two reds. index_row_bound read rows_misordered=1 on the open day shelf -- a peer's row above an older stamp, the %440 class -- and tools/fixtures/i/index_shelf_repair.sh sorted it in one command.
think stash_record read records_unlanded=1. stash@{0}, parked by fleet_round_open at 20260907.183139, held a whole finished lap: a plant-family repair across three files, its card block, its REDS row, its shelf, and its log. The log stood in no branch at all.
think I recovered the RECORD only -- git checkout "stash@{0}" -- <path>, which reads the tree so the mode rides -- because the guard's own header says the way to turn it green is to put the record back in the channel. The WORK half stays parked and is named here rather than half-landed: a tool change without its ledger row is worse than a parked one.
think The recovered record is not incidental. It carries the %574 measurement Petrichor's block asks Keaton for without a number: over 120 front doors the widened Reach moves 83, mean +3.66 composite, minimum -10, maximum +25, ZERO falling below B and 15 rising to it; a 140-page Field sample moves 25, mean -0.04.
think Then the rota row itself. Aether asks what the work is saying underneath, so I ran the doorway census the baton's own clause was written for. It answered RED: 38 pages name no room against a ceiling of 37.
think The ceiling was published at its own reading, so ONE page written without a token reds every ship's cold open. It runs tier cadence, so the hand that meets the refusal is not the hand that earned it -- a stranger, up to five rounds later. That is the shape, and it is why the census regrew twice from hand repairs.
think Measured before repairing: 846 post-seating door lines carry mixed 334 times, vision 268, checkable 149, research-for-understanding 84. mixed is the commonest because a design essay reasoning from measured readings toward a proposal is both registers at once.
think 29 living pages were repaired the way the elder +11 move was: each page's own opening sentence already asserted its register, and the token was transcribed into its door line beside whatever else that line said. No claim changed on any of the 29. mixed answered 24 times, vision once (a seated ruling no witness binds), research-for-understanding twice.
think The three that remain sit on active-designing/date/20260820/ and are dated testimony that accrete-never-break keeps as written, so 3 is a structural floor rather than a target. The ceiling stands there.
think THE MECHANISM BEHIND THE REGROWTH, which nobody had named: on 20260907.015907 a lap gave active-designing/README.md a "The room at the door" section, and that room has been silent-free since. The same lap recorded teaching the token in external-research/README.md's own Last updated line and left that body silent. The single page that landed between then and now came from that room.
obs A door that records teaching what it never says is a docs-implementation-sync fault in its purest form: the changelog line is the only place the claim lives. The repair is one bullet in the ritual list a writer actually reads before adding a page -- How To Add an Exploration -- rather than a hook.
obs Sample size one, said plainly. The mechanism is what recommends the repair, not the count.
obs docs/README.md is untouched on purpose: it supplies 14 pages, none of them silent, and it stands exactly at the 40 lines it declares, so adding the bullet would red declared_ceiling for no measured cause.
obs I did NOT build the write-time wall. At its floor the guard is a gate on new writing in a ratchet's clothes, and pre-commit reading only this commit's staged pages would put it at the author's desk and never red for a peer -- the narrow half of the question Bakery's withdrawn %524 wall framed this morning. Eight ships run that file and a peer landed rule six today. That call is Keaton's, and it is on the card.
obs Booking the row moved three ledger readings that no author writes: the headline census total 583 -> 584, its remainder 563 -> 564, and its span 1 to 583 -> 1 to 584. reds_ledger_monotone reds on all three until each is typed. That is the twelfth-odd firing of a repair a guard could derive.
obs The other two cold-open reds, plant and standing_equipment, came out of the same stash@{0}: an adoption count asserted as an equality, refusing the rise it exists to reward, raised by hand seven times in one day. The repair, its row and its log landed whole.
obs The parked row had booked %584, which the anointed spine also gave me. Its stamp 20260907.180000 is earlier than my 20260907.192800, so by the collision rule the earlier stamp keeps the number: it stands as %584 CLOSED and folded to its own shelf, and mine renumbered to %585. Neither was published, so no byte moved that a peer had seen -- the derived spine's class inside one tree, with no second host.
obs %569 met on metal, from the other side. Stopping my own hot runner before restarting it on a settled tree, I listed pids and read /proc/<pid>/cwd for each: 15 matched the pattern and exactly ONE was mine, the other 14 spread across patchouli, petrichor, pheromone, copal, diffuser and grass. A pkill -f would have stopped six peers' laps. The self-match half fired too -- my own pgrep shell answered the pattern twice and read as a surviving runner until I printed its args.
obs A small one, named rather than booked. Stopping the hot runner left construction/standing-equipment-run.lock.d behind, and the next pass refused with run_lock=in_flight pid=406886 while that pid was already dead. Its own advice reads "stop it with kill -TERM 406886, which runs this runner's own EXIT trap" -- against a corpse -- and the line beside it says a bypassed trap leaves the lock "for the next pass to reap", where the next pass refuses instead. A hand rmdir cleared it. Whether the runner should reap a lock whose pid is gone is one question and not this lap's.
obs %513's citation half paid for itself inside the hour. The hot pass red unshared_citation at 2: the card spelled both new numbers, and shared_max on the anointed spine is 583. Rewriting both as stamps cost two lines, where the elder habit would have spread them across the card, the log, the shelf and the commit body before anybody noticed.
obs The card came back 509 bytes over its bound and took six shaving passes to fit; it stands at 40,905 of 40,960, with 55 bytes of headroom. Three standing questions dropped to the shelf to make room -- the mycelium Door-negatives reading, the shared-pen repair, and rule_twin's drift ceiling -- each one click away, none retired.
